      <memberdef kind="function" id="group__xnvm__client__apis_1gab77cfbb4940f3923c7b721175d46f056" prot="public" static="no" const="no" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>int</type>
        <definition>int XNvm_GetServerLibInfo</definition>
        <argsstring>(XNvm_ClientInstance *InstancePtr, Xil_LibInfo *LibInfo)</argsstring>
        <name>XNvm_GetServerLibInfo</name>
        <param>
          <type>XNvm_ClientInstance *</type>
          <declname>InstancePtr</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>Xil_LibInfo *</type>
          <declname>LibInfo</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function sends an IPI request to get the XilNvm library version and capability bits running on the PLM. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>InstancePtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the client instance </para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>LibInfo</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to Xil_LibInfo. LibVersion and Capability are filled on success. The Version and NistStatus fields are reserved for XilNvm and must be ignored.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS If the library information is read successfully</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_INVALID_PARAM If any input parameter is invalid</para></listitem><listitem><para>XST_FAILURE If there is a failure </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Perform input parameter validation. Return XST_INVALID_PARAM if input parameters are invalid.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para><para>Query library info via the Features command using a valid NVM api-id as the selector, so the command succeeds and the server returns the library version/capability at fixed indices.</para><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Send request using generic API, the server returns the library version and capability bits along with the status of the command.</para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>        </inbodydescription>
